            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Equate the combined cost of the two coffee masses to the cost of 1 kg of the blend.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $x$ kg be the mass of type $A$. Then the mass of type $B$ is $(1-x)$ kg. The combined cost is $\\$15$.\n$$\\begin{align*}13x+18(1-x)&=15\\\\13x+18-18x&=15\\\\18-5x&=15\\\\18&=15+5x\\\\3&=5x\\\\x&=\\frac35\\end{align*}$$\nType $A$: $\\frac35\\times1000=600$ g.\n\nType $B$: $\\left(1-\\frac35\\right)\\times1000=400$ g.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
